<.shell title="Filter a list" current={:filter_a_list}>
  <h1>Filter a list</h1>
  <p class="lead">The activity list: filters, a summary line, the table, and pages.</p>

  <div class="example">
    <form class="filter-form" onsubmit="return false">
      <.input id="f-q" name="q" label="Search" value="" />
      <.input
        id="f-kind"
        name="activity"
        type="select"
        label="Kind"
        options={[
          {"All", "all"},
          {"Incident", "incident"},
          {"Exercise", "exercise"},
          {"Event", "event"}
        ]}
        value="all"
      />
      <.input
        id="f-when"
        name="when"
        type="select"
        label="When"
        options={[{"All", "all"}, {"Current", "current"}, {"Past", "past"}, {"2025", "2025"}]}
        value="2025"
      />
      <.input
        id="f-sort"
        name="sort"
        type="select"
        label="Sort"
        options={[{"Date ↓", "date-"}, {"Date ↑", "date"}]}
        value="date-"
      />
    </form>
    <div class="table-summary">
      <span class="table-summary-links">
        <.a href="#">Current</.a>
        ·
        <.a href="#">Future</.a>
        ·
        <.a href="#">Past</.a>
        ·
        <.a href="#">All</.a>
      </span>
      <span class="table-summary-count">1,912 activities</span>
    </div>
    <.activity_table
      id="sample-activities"
      rows={activities()}
      sort="date-"
      path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end}
      team={sample_team()}
    />
    <.pagination class="my-p" paginated={sample_page()} path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end} />
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Filters sit in a row above the table, with small inputs. Changing one updates the list.
    </li>
    <li>The summary line has quick links on the left and the count on the right.</li>
    <li><a href={page_path(:pagination)}>Pagination</a> goes under the table.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;.activity_filter_table&gt;</code>. Filters are <code>&lt;.input&gt;</code>s in a <code>.filter-form</code>, and the table is <code>&lt;.activity_table&gt;</code>, shown here with made-up activities.
  </p>
</.shell>
